# Bias, Ethics and Privacy

## 1. Lesson Goals

By the end of this lesson, students should be able to:

- explain what bias means in machine learning
- distinguish data bias, algorithm/model bias, and human/social bias
- explain how biased training data can lead to unfair predictions
- identify examples of bias in real-world machine learning systems
- explain ethical concerns linked to machine learning
- discuss fairness, accountability, transparency, explainability, and human oversight
- explain privacy risks when collecting and using data for machine learning
- explain data minimization, consent, anonymization, pseudonymization, retention, and access control
- explain why sensitive data needs stronger protection
- identify risks of using proxy variables
- explain why high-stakes ML decisions need careful review
- recommend ways to reduce bias, ethical risk, and privacy risk
- answer exam-style questions about bias, ethics, and privacy in ML

