## 38. Scenario Answer Bank

### If Asked: “Explain bias in ML”

```text
Bias in ML occurs when the data, labels, features, model design, or use context systematically produces inaccurate or unfair outcomes for certain people or groups.
```

### If Asked: “Explain why biased data is a problem”

```text
The model learns patterns from training data. If the training data is biased, incomplete, or unrepresentative, the model may learn biased patterns and make unfair or inaccurate predictions.
```

### If Asked: “Explain privacy risk”

```text
ML systems may collect and process personal or sensitive data. If too much data is collected, used without consent, stored too long, or poorly protected, users may suffer privacy harm or data breach.
```

### If Asked: “Recommend controls”

```text
The system should use representative data, evaluate performance across groups, minimize personal data collection, protect data with access control and encryption, provide human oversight, and allow review or appeal of important decisions.
```

### If Asked: “Why human oversight?”

```text
Human oversight is important because ML predictions can be wrong, biased, hard to explain, or missing context. Humans can review high-risk decisions and reduce harm.
```

