## 39. Common Misconceptions

| Mistake | Why it is wrong | Better understanding |
|---|---|---|
| ML is objective because it uses data | data can contain bias | models can reproduce unfair patterns |
| Removing sensitive fields removes all bias | proxy variables may remain | check indirect features |
| High accuracy means fair model | groups may have different error rates | evaluate across groups |
| Privacy only matters for names | indirect data can identify people | protect personal and sensitive data |
| Anonymization always removes all risk | re-identification can be possible | anonymize carefully |
| Ethics only matters after deployment | ethics should be considered from design stage | build responsibly |
| Human oversight is unnecessary if model is accurate | model can still be wrong or biased | review high-stakes decisions |
| More data is always better | more biased data can worsen bias | quality and representativeness matter |
| Users do not need to know ML is used | transparency matters | provide meaningful information |
| Accountability belongs to the computer | humans/organizations are responsible | define responsibility |

